  "description": "Overview: Get ready for a Competitive Programming showdown where speed, accuracy, teamwork, and strategy come together. Whether you are an experienced competitive programmer or relatively new to CP, the competition offers multiple ways to contribute and make an impact. The competition unfolds across three stages: a fast-paced Competitive Programming Round, a Non-Technical Challenge, and the Grand CP Finale. But there is a twist. Your performance in the earlier stages can directly influence your advantage in the finale. Every second, every decision, and every problem counts. Guidelines: Team Size: 2 participants Inter-College Teams: Allowed Round 1: Fast-paced CP round featuring easy-to-medium difficulty problems Qualification: Top 30 teams advance to Round 2 Round 2: 30-minute Challenge consisting of puzzles, quizzes, and other challenges Round 3: Grand CP Finale where both teammates compete individually and strategically use the advantages earned in Round 2 Detailed instructions and rules for each round will be announced before the respective round begins. Rules: Each participant may be a member of only one team. Plagiarism, copying, solution sharing, or any form of collaboration outside the permitted team structure is strictly prohibited. Participants must follow all instructions and guidelines issued by the organizers. Any form of unfair assistance, cheating, or misconduct may result in immediate disqualification. All submissions must be made through the designated contest platform. Participants are responsible for ensuring that their submissions comply with the rules of the respective round. The organizers reserve the right to disqualify participants or teams found violating the rules. The organizers' decision regarding qualification, scoring, penalties, and disqualification shall be final and binding.",
