    "details": "<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<p>Get ready for a Competitive Programming showdown where speed, accuracy, teamwork, and strategy come together.</p>\n<p>Whether you are an experienced competitive programmer or relatively new to CP, the competition offers multiple ways to contribute and make an impact.</p>\n<p>The competition unfolds across three stages: a fast-paced Competitive Programming Round, a Non-Technical Challenge, and the Grand CP Finale.</p>\n<p>But there is a twist.</p>\n<p>Your performance in the earlier stages can directly influence your advantage in the finale. Every second, every decision, and every problem counts.</p>\n<p><strong>Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team Size: 2 participants</li>\n<li>Inter-College Teams: Allowed</li>\n<li>Round 1: Fast-paced CP round featuring easy-to-medium difficulty problems</li>\n<li>Qualification: Top 30 teams advance to Round 2</li>\n<li>Round 2: 30-minute Challenge consisting of puzzles, quizzes, and other challenges</li>\n<li>Round 3: Grand CP Finale where both teammates compete individually and strategically use the advantages earned in Round 2</li>\n<li>Detailed instructions and rules for each round will be announced before the respective round begins.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each participant may be a member of only one team.</li>\n<li>Plagiarism, copying, solution sharing, or any form of collaboration outside the permitted team structure is strictly prohibited.</li>\n<li>Participants must follow all instructions and guidelines issued by the organizers.</li>\n<li>Any form of unfair assistance, cheating, or misconduct may result in immediate disqualification.</li>\n<li>All submissions must be made through the designated contest platform.</li>\n<li>Participants are responsible for ensuring that their submissions comply with the rules of the respective round.</li>\n<li>The organizers reserve the right to disqualify participants or teams found violating the rules.</li>\n<li>The organizers' decision regarding qualification, scoring, penalties, and disqualification shall be final and binding.</li>\n</ul>",
